    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d39b41b-36f1-4bc5-871b-06d424310938\n\nWhen completing `vim.loader` there are scenario's where mini.completion does not offer `loader`:\n\n1. Type `vim.`, wait a little, and continue with `l`. No `loader` yet in menu. Now type `o` and the `loader` pops up.\n2. Type `vim.`, wait a  little, and type `loa` very fast.\n3. EDIT... Type `vim.` and escape. Type `al` and notice that `loader` is present.\n\nAs can be seen in the video, `nvim-cmp` does offer the completion.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>init.lua</summary>\n \n```lua\n\nlocal function clone(path_to_site)\n  local mini_path = path_to_site .. \"pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\n  if not vim.uv.fs_stat(mini_path) then\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL\")\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function setup_cmp(cmp_sources)\n  local cmp = require(\"cmp\")\n  cmp.setup({\n    snippet = {\n      expand = function(args) -- mini.snippets expands snippets from lsp...\n        ---@diagnostic disable-next-line: undefined-global\n        MiniSnippets.default_insert({ body = args.body }) -- Insert at cursor\n      end,\n    },\n    sources = cmp.config.sources(cmp_sources),\n    mapping = cmp.mapping.preset.insert(),\n    completion = { completeopt = \"menuone,noinsert\" },\n  })\nend\n\nlocal function setup_mini()\n  require(\"mini.completion\").setup({\n    auto_setup = false,\n    source_func = \"omnifunc\",\n  })\n  if vim.fn.has(\"nvim-0.11\") == 1 then vim.opt.completeopt:append(\"fuzzy\") end\n  MiniDeps.later(function() MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind() end)\nend\n\nlocal path_to_site = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/\"\nclone(path_to_site)\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup({ path = { package = path_to_site } })\n\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\nlocal use_cmp = false\nMiniDeps.now(function()\n  require(\"mini.basics\").setup()\n  vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"randomhue\")\n\n  require(\"mini.icons\").setup()\n  require(\"mini.notify\").setup()\n  require(\"mini.snippets\").setup() -- only using lsp snippets\n  if use_cmp then\n    MiniDeps.add({ source = \"hrsh7th/nvim-cmp\", depends = { \"hrsh7th/cmp-nvim-lsp\" } })\n    setup_cmp({ { name = \"nvim_lsp\" } })\n  else\n    setup_mini()\n  end\n\n  MiniDeps.add(\"williamboman/mason.nvim\")\n  MiniDeps.add(\"williamboman/mason-lspconfig.nvim\")\n  MiniDeps.add(\"neovim/nvim-lspconfig\")\n  require(\"mason\").setup()\n  require(\"mason-lspconfig\").setup({ ensure_installed = { \"lua_ls\" } })\n  require(\"lspconfig\").lua_ls.setup({\n    on_attach = function(client, buf_id)\n      if not use_cmp then vim.bo[buf_id].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\" end\n    end,\n    settings = {\n      Lua = {\n        completion = { callSnippet = \"Replace\", keywordSnippet = \"Replace\" },\n        diagnostics = { globals = { \"vim\", \"MiniDeps\" } },\n        runtime = { version = \"LuaJIT\" },\n        telemetry = { enable = false },\n        workspace = {\n          ignoreSubmodules = true,\n          checkThirdParty = false,\n          library = {\n            vim.env.VIMRUNTIME,\n            \"${3rd}/luv/library\",\n            \"$XDG_DATA_HOME/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua\",\n          },\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  })\n  require(\"mini.statusline\").setup({})\nend)\n    \n```\n</details>\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\nNote: after reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n",
