        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am afraid I can not reproduce. Here is the demo using the exact copy-paste of the repro config:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce85e526-f3ef-4bb6-84e0-adf0f23646d2\n\nIn particular:\n- It returns `loader` entry on the first response, i.e. at `vim.`. Both slow and fast typing will show it.\n- It *doesn't* show the `go` (maybe others) on the first response and supplies that list is `isIncomplete` (i.e. next key press needs to send another request). After typing `g` (i.e. with line `vim.g`) 'mini.completion' makes another request and it *still* doesn't contain `go` in the response (I verified by logging the actual LSP server response) and the response still has `isIncomplete`. Only after typing `o` (i.e. with the line `vim.go`) it returns a list that contains `go` as an entry and the response has `isIncomplete = false`.\n\nI am not sure why there is different completion items on different systems. Maybe has something to do with performance, i.e. LuaLS (version 3.13.9 according to Mason, by the way) can supply more items in the same time span on my system.\n\nBut I can see that not suggesting `go` at the point of `vim.g` is indeed a 'mini.completion' issue: it makes LSP request for `isIncomplete` immediately inside `InsertCharPre` event. This results into request still being done for `vim.` and not `vim.g`. I'll take a look.",
